DELETE FROM kb_planet_in_sign WHERE planet = 'North Node';

INSERT INTO kb_planet_in_sign (planet, sign, summary, life_patterns, relationships, challenges, growth, book_references) VALUES
('North Node', 'Aries', 'You''re learning to claim your own desires and stand alone. After lifetimes of disappearing into others'' needs, your evolution demands you develop courage, assertion, and a strong sense of self. This feels selfish because you''re used to self-sacrifice—but it''s actually necessary.', 'You''re drawn to situations where you can test your independence and courage. You keep encountering circumstances that force you to choose between what others want and what you want. Your life gradually teaches you that your desires matter and that conflict is not catastrophic.', 'Partnerships feel uncomfortable because you''re learning that true connection requires two whole people, not a caretaker and a dependent. You''re discovering that wanting your own life doesn''t make you uncaring. Others often pull heavily on you, and learning to disappoint people is your primary relationship lesson.', 'You battle the impulse to keep the peace at all costs. You''re terrified of being seen as selfish or aggressive. The discomfort of asserting yourself runs deep—speaking up feels dangerous, even when nothing bad happens. Self-doubt and people-pleasing are your recurring traps.', 'As you develop authentic assertiveness, you become genuinely magnetic. People respect the person who knows what they want. Your growth isn''t about becoming aggressive; it''s about honoring your own integrity. You''re learning that courage and kindness can coexist.', ARRAY['Schulman, Karmic Astrology: The Moon''s Nodes and Reincarnation']),

('North Node', 'Taurus', 'You''re learning to build something real and enduring after lifetimes of chaos and intensity. Your growth lies in stability, patience, and the sensual grounding of the physical world. You''re being asked to slow down, enjoy what you have, and create security—not drama.', 'Your life teaches you the value of simple, steady progress. You''re drawn to building tangible things: savings accounts, gardens, skills, stable relationships. You encounter repeated lessons about the cost of crisis-seeking and the peace of routine. Comfort, when you finally allow it, becomes your teacher.', 'You''re learning that love doesn''t require constant intensity or transformation. Steady, reliable partners feel boring until you understand that they offer something precious: trust. You''re discovering that loyalty and presence are more valuable than the magnetic pull of chaos. Sensual connection grounds you.', 'Your attraction to deep transformation and psychological intensity keeps you in turbulent situations. You struggle to stay with anything boring, including good people. The stability you need feels tedious. You fear that peace means stagnation, so you sometimes create unnecessary drama to feel alive.', 'Your peace comes from learning that real power is building something that lasts. Sensual pleasures, financial security, and consistent relationships become sources of genuine fulfillment. You discover that depth can be found in consistency, not just crisis. Presence becomes your superpower.', ARRAY['Schulman, Karmic Astrology: The Moon''s Nodes and Reincarnation']),

('North Node', 'Gemini', 'You''re learning to listen, gather information, and honor multiple perspectives after lifetimes of preaching certainty. Your growth demands intellectual humility: admitting what you don''t know, asking genuine questions, and changing your mind based on new information. This contradicts your natural authority.', 'You keep encountering situations where your single viewpoint isn''t enough. You''re drawn to learning, conversation, and intellectual exploration. Life teaches you that understanding the other side doesn''t weaken your position—it strengthens it. Curiosity becomes your primary tool for evolution.', 'You''re learning that listening is an act of love. Partners need you to hear them, not just convince them. Your growth involves genuine interest in how others think and feel. You discover that connection deepens when you ask questions rather than deliver pronouncements.', 'You know too much and listen too little. Your certainty alienates people. You''re impatient with complexity and resistant to changing your mind. The humility required to say "I don''t know" or "you''re right" feels impossible. You often talk more than you listen.', 'Your real authority emerges from genuine knowledge, which requires listening first. As you become curious rather than certain, people actually hear you. You discover that flexibility is not weakness. Communication becomes a dance rather than a platform, and your influence deepens.', ARRAY['Schulman, Karmic Astrology: The Moon''s Nodes and Reincarnation']),

('North Node', 'Cancer', 'You''re learning vulnerability, emotional truth, and the courage of sensitivity after lifetimes of achievement and control. Your growth demands you feel instead of just accomplish, nurture instead of just produce, and let others matter more than your goals. This undoes everything you''ve built yourself on.', 'Life keeps softening you. You encounter losses, dependencies, and emotional needs that your productivity cannot fix. You''re drawn to family, home, and nurturing situations. Gradually you understand that intimacy requires showing up emotionally, not just practically. Your heart becomes your primary responsibility.', 'Relationships require emotional availability that doesn''t come naturally. You''re learning that people need your presence and vulnerability, not just your provision. Partners feel neglected by your focus on achievement. Your growth involves prioritizing connection over accomplishment.', 'You believe emotions are inefficient. You''re uncomfortable with your own needs and others'' feelings. The vulnerability required for real intimacy terrifies you. You armor yourself with work and responsibility, using these as excuses to stay emotionally distant. Admitting you need someone feels weak.', 'As you allow yourself to feel, your relationships transform. Vulnerability becomes your strength, not your liability. You discover that a well-lived life includes care, family, and emotional truth. Your achievement means nothing if you have no one to share it with.', ARRAY['Schulman, Karmic Astrology: The Moon''s Nodes and Reincarnation']),

('North Node', 'Leo', 'You''re learning to shine individually and claim authentic self-expression after lifetimes of hiding in groups. Your growth demands you step into visibility, take creative risks, and develop confidence in your own gifts. This means leaving the safety of the crowd and risking being seen.', 'You keep being drawn into situations where your individual voice and creativity are needed. Life gradually teaches you that your gifts are meant to be visible. You encounter repeated opportunities to shine, lead, or create. The spotlight, once your terror, becomes your teacher.', 'You''re learning that authentic connection requires showing your real self. Partners and friends need your genuine expression, not your acceptable performance. Your growth involves risking being truly seen. You discover that people love the real you more than the version that fits in.', 'You''re terrified of standing out or being judged. Conformity feels safer than authenticity. The ego it takes to put yourself forward feels wrong. You minimize yourself to avoid attention, even when you''re capable of excellence. Visibility triggers shame or fear of ridicule.', 'Your aliveness emerges when you express authentically. As you risk being visible, you discover your genuine confidence. People are drawn to your light, not repelled by it. Your creative gifts multiply when you stop hiding them. Leadership becomes possible because you''ve stopped pretending you''re less than you are.', ARRAY['Schulman, Karmic Astrology: The Moon''s Nodes and Reincarnation']),

('North Node', 'Virgo', 'You''re learning practical service, discrimination, and the power of perfecting small things after lifetimes of spiritual escapism. Your growth demands you show up in the physical world, do the unglamorous work, and serve through concrete action. This feels like losing yourself in details.', 'Life teaches you that the divine operates through dedication and precision. You''re drawn to learning practical skills, organizing systems, and serving through real work. You encounter repeated lessons about the value of showing up daily. Mastery becomes your teacher, not inspiration.', 'You''re learning that love is expressed through presence and practical care, not mystical understanding. Partners need you to remember things, follow through, and be reliable. Your growth involves being useful in small, unglamorous ways. Service becomes your highest spiritual practice.', 'You''re overwhelmed by mundane details and find them beneath you spiritually. You struggle with consistency, follow-through, and practical responsibility. The precision required to get things right feels tedious. You often float above the actual work, disappointed by reality''s messiness.', 'Your spiritual evolution manifests through dedicated craft and reliable service. As you embrace the practical world, you become genuinely helpful. Perfecting your skills becomes your spiritual path. You discover that humility and service are not beneath you—they''re your greatest teachers.', ARRAY['Schulman, Karmic Astrology: The Moon''s Nodes and Reincarnation']),

('North Node', 'Libra', 'You''re learning partnership, compromise, and the art of relationship after lifetimes of going it alone. Your growth demands you consider others'' needs equally with your own, negotiate instead of dictate, and find peace in mutual agreement. This feels like losing your autonomy.', 'Life keeps reflecting you to yourself through others. You''re drawn to partnerships that challenge your independence. You encounter repeated lessons about the wisdom in collaboration. Gradually you understand that true strength includes receiving from others. Connection becomes your teacher.', 'Relationships require genuine partnership where decisions aren''t yours alone. You''re learning that others'' feelings matter equally to yours. Real love involves compromise and seeing multiple perspectives. Your growth involves discovering that partnership is not surrender—it''s a higher expression of strength.', 'You default to independence and self-reliance. You struggle to ask for help or truly collaborate. The compromise required for partnership feels like weakness. You often run rather than work through conflict. Needing someone triggers your deepest fear of vulnerability.', 'Your peace emerges through genuine partnership. As you learn collaboration, life becomes more beautiful. Relationships become mirrors of your growth. You discover that interdependence is not weakness but the highest expression of maturity. Balance becomes your superpower.', ARRAY['Schulman, Karmic Astrology: The Moon''s Nodes and Reincarnation']),

('North Node', 'Scorpio', 'You''re learning depth, psychological truth, and transformation after lifetimes of staying comfortable and safe. Your growth demands you face what''s hidden, embrace power, and allow yourself to fundamentally change. This requires entering the darkness you''ve avoided.', 'Life gradually strips away your comforts and safety strategies. You''re drawn to deep psychological work and intense experiences. You encounter repeated invitations to transform and evolve. Darkness and depth, once your enemy, become your teacher. You learn that real strength includes facing what''s difficult.', 'Relationships require emotional depth and genuine honesty. You''re learning to show your shadow self and trust others with your truth. Partners need your real responses, not your nice ones. Your growth involves becoming comfortable with intensity, intimacy, and psychological complexity.', 'You retreat to comfort and superficial pleasures when things feel uncomfortable. You avoid confrontation and psychological depth. The intensity and honesty required for real intimacy feel too much. You cling to what''s familiar rather than embrace necessary transformation.', 'Your power emerges when you stop avoiding what''s real. As you become comfortable with depth and intensity, people trust you completely. Transformation becomes your superpower. You discover that facing your darkness makes you genuinely powerful and deeply relatable.', ARRAY['Schulman, Karmic Astrology: The Moon''s Nodes and Reincarnation']),

('North Node', 'Sagittarius', 'You''re learning to see the big picture and embrace expansive wisdom after lifetimes of getting lost in mental details. Your growth demands you develop faith, philosophy, and a broader vision of meaning. This requires leaving the safety of what you''ve already analyzed to death.', 'Life teaches you that not everything requires perfect knowledge. You''re drawn to travel, learning from experience, and exploring meaning. You encounter repeated lessons that the map is not the territory. Gradually you trust wisdom that can''t be proven. Direct experience becomes your teacher.', 'Relationships need your faith and vision, not your criticism. You''re learning to encourage others'' dreams instead of identifying problems. Partners need your optimism and belief in possibility. Your growth involves sharing a vision larger than individual concerns.', 'You get lost in details and cannot see the forest for the trees. You''re skeptical of anything that can''t be logically proven. The faith required for wisdom feels naive. You often overwhelm people with information and criticism instead of inspiration.', 'Your vision becomes clear when you stop analyzing everything. As you develop faith in something larger than yourself, life opens. Your wisdom flows through you to help others. You discover that living by principles rather than facts creates real meaning.', ARRAY['Schulman, Karmic Astrology: The Moon''s Nodes and Reincarnation']),

('North Node', 'Capricorn', 'You''re learning to build something concrete in the world and take your power seriously after lifetimes of staying safe at home. Your growth demands you step into authority, handle responsibility, and structure your ambitions into real achievement. This feels cold and disconnected from what matters.', 'Life pushes you into leadership whether you''re ready or not. You''re drawn to building, managing, and creating lasting structures. You encounter repeated responsibilities and opportunities to lead. Gradually you understand that building something real is your highest calling. Authority becomes your teacher.', 'Relationships need your commitment and reliability, not just your emotional presence. You''re learning that love includes showing up consistently and taking others seriously. Partners need to know they can count on you. Your growth involves balancing care with capability.', 'You''re overwhelmed by emotional needs and shy away from responsibility. The public world feels cold and your family feels like enough. The authority and visibility required for achievement feel wrong. You hide behind caregiving instead of claiming your real power.', 'Your peace comes from building something that lasts. As you step into authority, your natural leadership emerges. Responsibility becomes your freedom. You discover that supporting others'' growth means establishing yourself first. Legacy becomes your superpower.', ARRAY['Schulman, Karmic Astrology: The Moon''s Nodes and Reincarnation']),

('North Node', 'Aquarius', 'You''re learning to serve the collective and surrender individual glory after lifetimes of being the center. Your growth demands you develop detachment, idealism, and commitment to something bigger than yourself. This means becoming part of the group instead of its star.', 'Life gradually teaches you that individual achievement is hollow. You''re drawn to groups, causes, and movements. You encounter repeated lessons that real power serves the whole. Your significance emerges not from being special but from contributing something meaningful. The collective becomes your teacher.', 'Relationships need your intellectual engagement and shared vision, not just romantic intensity. You''re learning that true partnership includes friendship and shared ideals. Partners need you to be part of something bigger than the relationship. Your growth involves balancing intimacy with detachment.', 'You need to be the best, most important, or most special. The surrender required to serve the collective feels like erasure. You struggle with being ordinary or part of the group. Your need to be exceptional often isolates you from real community.', 'Your brilliance serves humanity when you release the need for individual recognition. As you join with others toward a common good, your gifts multiply. You discover that real power is invisible and collective. Your idealism becomes your greatest gift.', ARRAY['Schulman, Karmic Astrology: The Moon''s Nodes and Reincarnation']),

('North Node', 'Pisces', 'You''re learning to surrender, trust, and dissolve your need for control after lifetimes of managing every detail. Your growth demands you embrace mystery, develop compassion, and allow yourself to be held by something larger. This feels like chaos and loss of power.', 'Life teaches you that you cannot control what matters most. You''re drawn to spiritual practice, compassion, and transcendence. You encounter repeated situations where surrender, not strategy, is the answer. Gradually you trust that you''re held. Faith becomes your teacher.', 'Relationships need your compassion and surrender, not your perfect management. You''re learning to receive from others and allow imperfection. Partners need you to let go of how things "should" be. Your growth involves trusting the process rather than controlling the outcome.', 'You believe precision can fix everything. The uncertainty and messiness of life feels intolerable. You armor yourself with planning and control. The trust required for real surrender feels dangerous. You often suffocate relationships with your need to organize everything perfectly.', 'Your peace emerges when you stop fighting reality. As you surrender to what is, life flows. You discover that compassion and trust are more powerful than control. Your greatest gifts flow through you when you stop trying to direct them.', ARRAY['Schulman, Karmic Astrology: The Moon''s Nodes and Reincarnation']);
